1 Introduction
**************

Code Review shows a pull request in its own review buffer, such as
‘*Code Review: visor!4*’: its header (author, title, state, branches,
labels, assignees, reviewers), its commits, its description, the
conversation and the diff of every changed file, with the review
comments placed on the lines they were made on.  Outdated comments are
shown with the diff hunk they were made on.

   From that buffer you can:

   • read and reply to comments, and add comments to any line of the
     diff, including code suggestions;
   • approve, request changes or comment, with an overall feedback
     message;
   • set labels, assignees, milestones, reviewers, the title and the
     description;
   • react to comments with emoji, and promote a comment to a new issue;
   • review a single commit, save an unfinished review and resume it
     later;
   • visit a changed file in your local clone, or a binary file in
     Dired.

   Not every feature is available on every forge; *note Forge Support::.

1.1 About this fork
===================

This is a fork of <https://github.com/wandersoncferreira/code-review>,
which is unmaintained since December 2022 and no longer loads with
current versions of its dependencies.  The fork's ‘port’ branch:

   • ports the database layer to current EmacSQL and closql, and the
     Gitlab requests to current Ghub, which dropped ‘glab-get’ and
     similar functions;
   • removes Bitbucket support;
   • fixes Gitlab replies, approval and review feedback against current
     Gitlab, and reviews each merge request on its own Gitlab instance.

   Only Gitlab has been tested since the port, on gitlab.com and on a
self-hosted instance.  The Github code compiles but is untested.


