2 Installation
**************

Do not install ‘code-review’ from MELPA: that is the unported upstream
version.  Install the fork's ‘port’ branch with ‘package-vc’, which also
installs the dependencies from the package archives.  MELPA must be in
‘package-archives’.

     (package-vc-install
      '(code-review :url "https://github.com/ilitzroth/code-review"
                    :branch "port"))

   Or, from a local clone:

     (package-vc-install-from-checkout "~/path/to/code-review" "code-review")

   This manual comes with the package as ‘code-review.info’, with a
‘dir’ file next to it, at the top of the repository.  When the package
is installed with ‘package-vc-install’, the package directory is the
clone, so Emacs adds it to ‘Info-directory-list’ and the manual appears
in ‘C-h i’.  A package installed with ‘package-vc-install-from-checkout’
lives in a separate directory that only loads the clone's autoloads, so
add the clone yourself:

     (with-eval-after-load 'info
       (add-to-list 'Info-directory-list "~/path/to/code-review"))

   Then configure access to your forge: *note Gitlab::, or *note
Github::.


