7 Editing the Pull Request
**************************

The ‘Setters’ group of the Transient menu changes the pull request
itself.  These changes are sent right away.

‘r s r’
     Request reviews (‘code-review-request-reviews’).

‘r s y’
     Assign yourself (‘code-review-set-yourself-assignee’).

‘r s a’
     Set the assignee (‘code-review-set-assignee’).

‘r s m’
     Set the milestone (‘code-review-set-milestone’).  Github only sets
     it for users with push access, and silently ignores it otherwise.

‘r s l’
     Set the labels (‘code-review-set-label’).

‘r s t’
     Edit the title (‘code-review-set-title’).

‘r s d’
     Edit the description (‘code-review-set-description’).

   Labels, reviewers and other fields that take several values are read
with ‘completing-read-multiple’: separate the values with commas, and
press ‘TAB’ to see the candidates.  An empty input removes all labels.


