8 Reactions
***********

On Github you can react with emoji to the description and to any
comment.

   • Press ‘C-c C-r’ on a comment or the description to add a reaction.
   • Press ‘RET’ on an emoji to add your reaction or remove it.

   Each kind of comment has its own command, bound in its own keymap.
To use another key, rebind them:

     (define-key code-review-description-section-map (kbd "C-c C-r")
       #'code-review-description-reaction-at-point)
     (define-key code-review-code-comment-section-map (kbd "C-c C-r")
       #'code-review-code-comment-reaction-at-point)
     (define-key code-review-comment-section-map (kbd "C-c C-r")
       #'code-review-conversation-reaction-at-point)


File: code-review.info,  Node: Merging,  Next: Saving and Resuming Reviews,  Prev: Reactions,  Up: Top

9 Merging
*********

The ‘Merge’ group of the Transient menu merges the pull request on
Github: ‘r m m’ with a merge commit (‘code-review-merge-merge’), ‘r m r’
by rebasing (‘code-review-merge-rebase’) and ‘r m s’ by squashing
(‘code-review-merge-squash’).

   This is experimental.  The commit title and message are taken from
the pull request's title and description, and cannot be changed.


