15.1 Options
============

All options are in the customization group ‘code-review’, with its
subgroups ‘code-review-github’ and ‘code-review-gitlab’.

‘code-review-auth-login-marker’
     The symbol after ‘^’ in the login of your auth source entries.  The
     default is ‘code-review’; set it to ‘forge’ to use Forge's tokens.

‘code-review-fill-column’
     The column at which comments are wrapped; default 80.

‘code-review-new-buffer-window-strategy’
     The function that shows a new review buffer; default
     ‘switch-to-buffer-other-window’.

‘code-review-worktree-function’
     The function returning the directory in which to visit a pull
     request's files; default ‘code-review-checkout-in-clone’.  *Note
     Visiting Files::.

‘code-review-buffer-name’
‘code-review-commit-buffer-name’
‘code-review-comment-buffer-name’
     The names of the review, commit and comment buffers.  The name of a
     review buffer is ‘code-review-buffer-name’ followed by the
     repository and the number.

‘code-review-section-indent-width’
     The indentation of nested sections; default 1.

‘code-review-section-image-scaling’
     The scaling of images shown in the buffer; default 0.8.

‘code-review-lgtm-message’
     The message of ‘r l’; default ‘LGTM! :thumbsup:’.

‘code-review-always-restrict-approval?’
     If non-‘nil’, refuse approving a pull request with a failing CI
     state.

‘code-review-download-dir’
     The directory binary files are downloaded to; default
     ‘/tmp/code-review/’.

‘code-review-db-database-file’
     The database of reviews and local comments.

‘code-review-log-file’
     The file errors are logged to; *note Troubleshooting::.

‘code-review-log-raw-request-responses’
     If non-‘nil’, also log the raw responses of the forge.

‘code-review-headers-hook’
‘code-review-sections-hook’
‘code-review-sections-commit-hook’
     The functions that insert the header lines and the sections of the
     review buffer and of the commit buffer.  Remove a function to hide
     its section.

‘code-review-comment-buffer-msg’
‘code-review-comment-feedback-msg’
‘code-review-comment-single-comment-msg’
‘code-review-comment-suggestion-msg’
     The help texts at the top of the comment buffer.

   The forge hosts are described in *note Gitlab Instances:: and *note
Github Enterprise::.

   To show emoji such as ‘:thumbsup:’ as symbols, enable ‘emojify-mode’:

     (add-hook 'code-review-mode-hook #'emojify-mode)


