15.2 Key Binding Suggestions
============================

Bind ‘code-review-forge-pr-at-point’ in Forge's buffers, on a pull
request in a Magit status buffer and in a pull request's own buffer:

     (with-eval-after-load 'forge
       (define-key forge-pullreq-mode-map (kbd "C-c r")
         #'code-review-forge-pr-at-point)
       (define-key forge-pullreq-section-map (kbd "C-c r")
         #'code-review-forge-pr-at-point))

   Or bind it to ‘/’, which Magit leaves free, in all Magit buffers, and
add it to Magit's dispatch menu (‘?’) next to Forge's ‘N’.  The
‘:inapt-if-not’ greys the entry out when point is not on a pull request:

     (with-eval-after-load 'forge
       (define-key magit-mode-map (kbd "/")
         #'code-review-forge-pr-at-point)
       (transient-append-suffix 'magit-dispatch "N"
         '("/" "Code review" code-review-forge-pr-at-point
           :inapt-if-not forge-current-pullreq)))

   Delete local comments and the feedback with ‘k’:

     (define-key code-review-feedback-section-map (kbd "k")
       #'code-review-section-delete-comment)
     (define-key code-review-local-comment-section-map (kbd "k")
       #'code-review-section-delete-comment)
     (define-key code-review-reply-comment-section-map (kbd "k")
       #'code-review-section-delete-comment)

   Move between comments with ‘C-c n’ and ‘C-c p’.  Not ‘C-c C-n’: on a
comment, that promotes it to an issue.

     (define-key code-review-mode-map (kbd "C-c n")
       #'code-review-comment-jump-next)
     (define-key code-review-mode-map (kbd "C-c p")
       #'code-review-comment-jump-previous)

   The submit commands, such as ‘code-review-submit-approve’, can also
be bound directly, but the Transient menu shows what is available.


